updated: 2026-10-18T06:32:30Z
---

The default IO backend is `Kubernetes::REST::LWPIO` (LWP::UserAgent). cpanfile requires `LWP::UserAgent` and `IO::Socket::SSL` but not `LWP::Protocol::https`, which has been a separate distribution since libwww-perl 6 and is not a hard prerequisite of it. `grep -rn 'Protocol::https' lib cpanfile dist.ini README.md` finds nothing. On a perl that only got `cpanm Kubernetes::REST`, every request to an `https://` endpoint - i.e. every real cluster - comes back as LWP's internal 501 'Protocol scheme 'https' is not supported (LWP::Protocol::https not installed)', surfaced as `Kubernetes API error (...): 501`. Same class of gap Net::Async::Kubernetes 0.009 just closed for IO::Async::SSL. Dependants (MCP::K8s, Kubernetes::Comb) inherit it.

Done when: `requires 'LWP::Protocol::https';` is in cpanfile with a Changes line. Optional: make the 501-internal case croak with a hint instead of looking like an API error.

